                                "text": "1640-41, Ben Jonson, A Sonnet, to the Noble Lady, the Lady Mary Wroth,\nI that have been a lover, and could show it/ Though not in these, in rhymes not wholly dumb/ Since I exscribe your sonnets, am become/ A better lover, and much better poet."
